      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "ComputerObserve",
          "kind": "step",
          "title": "Observe",
          "description": "Observe the parts inside a computer's system unit and what each one does.",
          "imageName": null,
          "autoplayVO": true,
          "voClip": "ICT_Computer_Observe",
          "captions": [
            {
              "text": "A computer is made of parts that work together. They take in data, process it, store it, and give out information.",
              "duration": 9.954
            },
            {
              "text": "Most of these parts live inside the system unit. Let's take off the side panel and look inside.",
              "duration": 8.322
            },
            {
              "text": "The large circuit board at the back is the motherboard. Every other part connects to it, so they can share power and data.",
              "duration": 9.402
            },
            {
              "text": "In the middle is the central processing unit, or CPU. It carries out instructions and does calculations. It is the brain of the computer.",
              "duration": 11.754
            },
            {
              "text": "The CPU gets hot as it works, so a heat sink and fan sit on top of it to carry the heat away.",
              "duration": 7.53
            },
            {
              "text": "Beside the CPU are the memory modules, called RAM. RAM holds the programs and data the computer is using right now.",
              "duration": 9.786
            },
            {
              "text": "RAM is volatile. When the power goes off, everything in it is lost.",
              "duration": 6.786
            },
            {
              "text": "Programs and files are kept for a long time on drives, like this solid-state drive and this hard disk drive. They keep their data even without power.",
              "duration": 11.562
            },
            {
              "text": "The graphics card turns data into the pictures you see on the monitor.",
              "duration": 5.634
            },
            {
              "text": "The power supply unit changes electricity from the wall socket into the steady, low voltages the parts need.",
              "duration": 7.818
            },
            {
              "text": "Fans keep the air moving through the case, so all the parts stay cool.",
              "duration": 5.85
            },
            {
              "text": "Together, these parts let the computer do its work. Now it is your turn to take them out.",
              "duration": 8.034
            },
            {
              "text": "Select Next to continue.",
              "duration": -1
            }
          ],
          "buttons": [
            {
              "id": "observe_replay",
              "text": "Replay",
